.aider*
*.lock

# Timestamped backups written by the various *-set / toggle scripts before they
# rewrite a config in place. Useful locally for an undo, but they are snapshots
# of generated state and shouldn't be versioned -- git already is the backup.
*.bak.*

# Ghostty per-machine OS include, created by `make ghostty` (uname-selected)
.config/ghostty/os/active
# Active theme selection, created by `make theme` / `theme-set` (per-machine)
.config/themes/active
__pycache__/

# Electron runtime state that Slack drops into whatever directory it was
# launched from -- which, once, was this one. The Singleton* entries are
# symlinks into /run/user and a PID-named lock, so they are already dangling;
# userData/ is its per-user profile. All of it is machine-local and recreated
# on demand.
SingletonCookie
SingletonLock
SingletonSocket
userData/
